Email signature images, served by direct URL only.

They are deliberately not referenced from any page, component, sitemap or
navigation. robots.txt disallows the folder.

One thing is still outstanding: Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy is same-origin
site wide (see netlify.toml), which makes a browser refuse these when the page
asking for them is on another origin — which an email signature always is.
Gmail is unaffected because it fetches through its own proxy server side.
Apple Mail and Outlook on the web ask the browser directly and will show a
broken image until /signature/* is allowed cross-origin.
